QuestGuidance.Register("en",435,{
[13889]="7006E966\n1\tComplete an Umbar or Ikorbân raid on any tier\tThe evils within The Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo and The Temple of Utug-bûr must be stopped. Complete one raid on any tier.\n2\tReturn to the Temple of Utug-bûr Quartermaster\tReturn to the Temple of Utug-bûr Quartermaster with proof of your victory.\n",
[13890]="7005338E\n1\tBurn banners of vengeance at Lúlstrok (total: 8)\tBanners of vengeance can be found at Lúlstrok in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields. You have discovered the cruel banners of Mazog being flown by the Shapag-hai. You should burn them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many of the cruel banners flown in Mazog's name by the Shapag-hai.\n",
[13891]="700272AC\n1\tAccompany Andreg to the Slade of Shadows\tAndreg awaits you near the Slade of Shadows. You should speak with Andreg when you are ready to put his plan in motion. WARNING: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.\n2\tBring the tokens of the gurach to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tSaeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp, north of the Slade of Shadows. You should return to Saeradan with the news of Andreg's sacrifice at the Slade of Shadows.\n",
[13892]="7002C914\n1\tCollect red aster for the tribute (total: 5)\tRed aster may be collected north of Frithstan's camp, scattered around Aster Hill. Penda has asked you to collect red aster, a bright flower that blooms in the Wailing Hills.\n2\tPlace the flowers at the base of the Cuthstan\tThe memorial location is at the base of the Cuthstan, atop the large hill where Lanbert's camp may be found. The flowers may be placed at the memorial site in order to pay respect to all those honourable warriors who have passed on.\n",
[13893]="700219B8\n1\tTalk to Gronu at his camp\tGronu is at his camp, north of Harndirion. You should return to Gronu and tell him that the Draig-lûth have been gathering supplies near Amon Mîn.\n",
[13894]="70008879\n1\tReturn to Quartermaster Apsduf at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect legs of Men (total: 10)\tMen can be found throughout the Ettenmoors. Quartermaster Apsduf ordered you to gather Man-flesh as tribute to the Tyrant at Tol Ascarnen.\n",
[13895]="700398DF\n1\tAid Folcbur\030Aid Déorwald\030Aid Béored\tFolcbur, Déorwald, and Béored can be found at the traders' pavillion in central Middlemead. Hildulf has asked you to aid the traders with troubles they have brought to his attention. You should speak to the traders nearby to learn of their plights.\n2\tTalk to Hildulf\tHildulf can be found at the traders' pavillion in central Middlemead. You have aided the traders of Middlemead with their troubles, and should now report your success to Hildulf.\n3\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found inside the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have aided the traders and spoken to Hildulf. Hildulf has asked you to speak to Thane Mágla.\n4\tEscort Hildulf to the Mead Hall of Middlemead\tHildulf can be found at the traders' pavillion in central Middlemead. Thane Mágla has asked you to bring Hildulf to the Mead Hall to answer about suspicious happenings in and around Middlemead.\n5\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead. Hildulf has vanished from Middlemead, and cannot be found. You should return to Mágla with this news.\n",
[13896]="70052980\n1\tCollect mushrooms (total: 8)\tMushrooms can be found north of the Beorninghús. You should gather mushrooms for Sterkist.\n2\tBring the mushrooms to Sterkist\tSterkist can be found at the Beorninghús. You should bring the mushrooms to Sterkist.\n",
[13897]="7002FCF3\n1\tKill Wargs at Fang Point (total: 8)\tWargs can be found in and around Fang Point in the Wold. You should search Fang Point for the Wargs that prowl the roads, making travel dangerous for all who venture into the Wold.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of vicious Wargs at Fang Point, making the roads safer for all who travel in the Wold between Harwick and the Norcrofts.\n",
[13898]="7004DCE3\n1\tCollect Jangovar trinkets for the ravens of Ravenhill (total: 14)\tTrinkets are carried by many of the Jangovar in the North. Dís has suggested that renewing the old practice of offering shiny trinkets to the ravens might aid in rebuilding a friendship between Durin's Folk and their kind.\n2\tDeliver the trinkets to Dís at Ravenhill\tDís can be found at Ravenhill. You have gathered many trinkets from the Jangovar and should now deliver them to Dís.\n",
[13899]="7001758B\n1\tBring the instrument to Pada\030Acquire the instrument from Shîk in the Foundations of Stone\tThe Orc Shîk can be found in the Foundations of Stone. Pada mentioned looking for Shîk in the pools of water with waterfalls along the northern edges of the Foundations of Stone. Pada has requested that you venture forth to recover an excellent and famous instrument from the unworthy Orcs to help further your final education as a Minstrel.\n",
[13900]="70027B12\n1\tTalk to Urdan\tUrdan is by the large war-machines on the eastern side of the Ring of Isengard. Morflak's lackey wants you to see if Urdan has anything that needs doing.\n2\tPick up a crate of tools\tUrdan wants you to fetch him a crate of tools from the anvil field north of Orthanc. He told you to follow the Ring-wall north to reach it.\n3\tTalk to Morflak's lackey\tMorflak's lackey wants to speak with you.\n",
[13901]="7000B332\n1\tSpeak with the ranger to enter mortal battle as a troll\tSpeak again to the ranger within this room and choose to enter battle as a savage troll out of Angmar.\n2\tSpeak with the ranger to complete the quest.\t\n",
[13902]="700173AE\n1\tDefeat Gazathrûg Handlers (total: 4)\tThe Grand Stair is north-east of the Orc-watch. The Uruk troll-handlers should be slain for the safety of the dwarves who have come to reclaim Khazad-dûm.\n2\tTalk to Ossur at the Orc-watch\tOssur the dwarf can be found at the Orc-watch. You defeated a good number of the Uruk troll-handlers, but the trolls were unmoved and did not begin attacking other tribes of Orcs within the Grand Stair.\n",
[13903]="7001CC66\n1\tDefeat Skûm at Durbúrz-stazg\tThe eastern gate of Durbúrz-stazg lies to the north of Echad Sirion. Tethafnel has asked you to defeat the Olog-hai warrior Skûm at Durbúrz-stazg. You will need to enter the encampment through the eastern gate.\n2\tTalk to Tethafnel at Echad Sirion\tEchad Sirion lies to the south of Durbúrz-stazg. You should return to Tethafnel with news of your victory against the olog-hai Skûm.\n",
[13904]="70019ECF\n1\tHunt in Angmar\tHunt in Angmar.\n",
[13905]="70019EBF\n1\tHunt in Eregion\tHunt in Eregion.\n",
[13906]="70019EC7\n1\tHunt in Forochel\tHunt in Forochel.\n",
[13907]="7002BFDD\n1\tSeek out evidence of trolls in the Brown Lands\tScouts claimed seeing trolls in the distance throughout the Brown Lands. Céola wants you to seek out evidence -- or the lack thereof -- of trolls in the Brown Lands.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. You should return to Céola and warn him that there are indeed trolls in the Brown Lands.\n",
[13908]="7000ABD1\n1\tPatrol the Ettenmoors\tPatrol the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13909]="7000AC06\n1\tPatrol the Ettenmoors\tPatrol the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13910]="7000B108\n1\tPatrol the Ettenmoors\tPatrol the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13911]="7000B109\n1\tPatrol the Ettenmoors\tPatrol the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13912]="7000B10A\n1\tPatrol the Ettenmoors\tPatrol the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13913]="7000B10B\n1\tPatrol the Ettenmoors\tPatrol the Ettenmoors.\n",
[13914]="70046C25\n1\tSearch for trolls to the north of Henneth Annûn\030Search for trolls to the south-west of Henneth Annûn\030Search for trolls to the north-west of Henneth Annûn\030Search for trolls to the north-east of Henneth Annûn\tTrolls might be found throughout North Ithilien, but especially near shaded areas. Ereblen has asked you to search for Trolls that may have taken refuge in North Ithilien after the Dawnless Day faded.\n2\tTalk to Ereblen\tEreblen can be found to the west of Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. You have discovered the last remaining troll in North Ithilien and defeated it. You should now return to Ereblen.\n",
[13915]="7003E432\n1\tScout the troll-cave in the Bruinen Gorges\tThe troll-cave lies to the north-east of Arrod's camp. Arrod asked you to scout the entrance to the troll-cave, which Caledhroval discovered, and and see what you can learn about their strength.\n2\tDefeat the spying hendroval\tThe hendroval can be found near the entrance to the troll-cave in the Bruinen Gorges, north-east of Arrod's camp. You should deal with the hendroval before it can warn the trolls.\n",
[13916]="7003EAF7\n1\tDefeat Stone-trolls in the North Trollshaws (total: 8)\tStone-trolls can be found at the ruins of Ost Belegram, south-west of Thoroniel's encampment. Thoroniel has asked you and your companions to deal with the Stone-trolls of the North Trollshaws.\n2\tTalk to Thoroniel\tThoroniel is posted north-east of Ost Belegram, in the North Trollshaws. You should return to Thoroniel and let her know that you have done as she has asked.\n",
[13917]="70000634\n1\tReturn trophies to Ted Reedy in Buckland\030Collect pristine bear-carcasses (total: 3)\030Collect pristine boar-heads (total: 3)\030Collect pristine wolf-carcasses (total: 3)\030Collect coarse bear-hides (total: 10)\tBears, boars, and wolves roam the Bree-fields north of Buckland, between the Brandy Hills and the border of the Old Forest. Ted Reedy has requested that you collect materials that will help to give Adso's Inn a rustic feel.\n",
[13918]="7005307F\n1\tCollect rock-worm scales\tRock-worms can be found on the northern edge of the Gladdenmere. You should collect scales from some of the rock-worms you defeat in the Gladdenmere.\n2\tCollect rock-worm scales (total: 10)\tRock-worms can be found on the northern edge of the Gladdenmere. You should collect scales from some of the rock-worms you defeat in the Gladdenmere.\n3\tBring the rock-worm scales to Varthmath in the Gladdenmere\tVarthmath can be found in the Gladdenmere. You should bring the scales to Varthmath.\n",
[13919]="7000839C\n1\tBring skull-amulets and bloodstone-pendants to Raith\030Collect skull-amulets (total: 6)\030Collect bloodstone-pendants (total: 4)\tThe fortress of Tór Gailvin is north-east of Aughaire, and its defenders carry the skull-amulets and bloodstone-pendants that Raith wants. Raith of Aughaire has asked you to wrest signs of the loyalty of the Trév Duvárdain to Angmar from the defenders of Tór Gailvin.\n",
[13920]="700272BD\n1\tCollect Orc-heads at Ak-ghru (total: 3)\tOrcs can be found at Ak-ghru. Elfrith asked you to collect Orc-heads as trophies to display as a warning to the Enemy in the Gravenwood.\n2\tBring the Orc-heads to Elfrith\tElfrith is hiding beyond the bounds of Ak-ghru. You should bring the heads you collected to Elfrith.\n",
})
